From a64748171bbb55da5b779dc7be689f6f0a7dd838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:35:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: "Automatic" of five Hades settings is Hades' own
 string, which Estuary translates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five Hades settings had Kodi's #36058 ("Automatic") as the label of their automatic option:
videoplayer.hades3dmvc, videoscreen.hades3doutput, videoscreen.hadeshdr10adapt,
videoscreen.hadesdvpathmode and videoscreen.hadesdvstepmode. Kodi's language add-ons that the
Piers repository serves (resource.language.es_ar 11.0.74, es_mx 11.0.85) leave #36058
untranslated, so in Spanish of Argentina and of Mexico those five lists showed "Automatic" in
English, while their help says "Automático".

They now use #39875, the "Automatic" of videoscreen.hadeshdrdepth, which the settings dialog maps
to Estuary #32116 (CGUIDialogSettingsBase::GetLocalizedString), translated "Automático" in
es_es, es_ar and es_mx. The English and the stored values do not change. The comments of #39875
and #32116 name the settings that use them.

Host tests (outside the tree): maptest (every text of a Hades setting is mapped to Estuary with
a translation), pairs, msgidsync, po-dups and idtable: no fault.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po    |  2 +-
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po        |  2 +-
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po        |  2 +-
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po        |  2 +-
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po        |  2 +-
 system/settings/settings.xml                           | 10 +++++-----
 6 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index ec99696..e440231 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -25639,7 +25639,7 @@ msgctxt "#39874"
 msgid "How many bits per colour the graphics card sends for HDR10 and HLG. Automatic (the default): as many as the TV and the picture mode allow, 10 or 12. 8 bits: never more than 8; some TVs with an 8-bit panel show less banding that way. SDR and native Dolby Vision are not affected. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
-#. Hades: value of the setting of the depth of HDR: as many bits as the display and the mode take
+#. Hades: value of the setting of the depth of HDR: as many bits as the display and the mode take; also the "Automatic" of the 3D MVC, 3D output, HDR10 adapted to the display, Dolby Vision drawing path and Dolby Vision fidelity step-down settings
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39875"
 msgid "Automatic"
